docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/08-spec-round3-codex.md:1:| # | Severity P1/P2/P3 | Section | Defect | Concrete fix |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/08-spec-round3-codex.md:3:| 1 | P1 | §2.1, §3.4 invariants 5 and 7 | **Valid published results fail reconciliation.** `classifyRegime` calculates margin from **unrounded** shares, then rounds it; F4 `marginPp` uses stored, rounded shares. The existing US fixture stores `11.023622`, while rounded shares produce `11.023600`; CN produces `28.333333` versus `28.333400`. Invariant 5 demands equality, and invariant 7 permits only `1e-6` difference. Both fixtures therefore lose their numbers despite being valid. | Reconstruct publisher arithmetic from stored weights/support in publisher order, without evaluating predicates. Validate snapshot margin against that result; separately validate F4 margin against F4’s rounded-share calculation. Add both existing fixtures as successful end-to-end clock cases. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/08-spec-round3-codex.md:4:| 2 | P1 | §3.4 invariant 1; §3.5 evidence | **A contribution can reference a comparison observation and still pass all checks.** Membership plus matching `series_id` does not establish that `contribution.observation_id` is the series’ latest observation. Replacing it with that series’ `prev` ID leaves arithmetic, rule support and F4 claim unchanged. The table/drawer nevertheless uses `rows[].latest`, so the displayed evidence differs from the stored contribution. | Require each contribution’s observation ID to equal the reconstructed frozen latest ID. Reject duplicate periods/ambiguous latest observations. Add a same-series previous-observation substitution test. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/08-spec-round3-codex.md:5:| 3 | P1 | §5.8 migration | **The adapter-constraint lookup is ambiguous.** `pg_get_constraintdef(oid) like '%adapter%'` matches both the adapter enum CHECK and `macro_evidence_path`, whose expression also references `adapter`. Non-STRICT `SELECT INTO` can select the wrong constraint. The old enum CHECK can remain, continuing to reject `official_http`, or adding the named replacement can fail. | Select the exact enum constraint by verified name or constrained column/expression identity; assert exactly one match. Preserve `macro_evidence_path`. Test the migration against the actual baseline schema and insert a valid `official_http` evidence object afterward. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/08-spec-round3-codex.md:6:| 4 | P1 | §5.7; §0.2 R-M39 | **“Do not change `macro-regime.v1.test.ts`” contradicts the mandatory registry switch.** That test explicitly requires `REGISTRY.filter(...)` to equal `[macroRegimeV1]`, uses live `CATALOG_VERSION` in expected historical claims, and compares the committed replay fixture with a builder using current formula hashes. Retiring v1 and changing its dependency files invalidates these assertions. A new fixture-hash comparison does not repair them. | Preserve the historical module and golden fixture, but explicitly migrate tests: isolate v1 with a historical registry/catalog/hash fixture; test the production registry and compensation separately against v2/v3. Do not regenerate the historical golden fixture from changed dependencies. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/08-spec-round3-codex.md:10:| 8 | P2 | §0.2 R-C14; §5.3, §5.5, §9 | **The claimed completion-witness disposition is not implemented by the design.** §0.2 promises separate “awaiting completion” and “no source data” states; §5.3 explicitly withdraws that UI requirement and §9 defers it. Existing monthly-derived rows have no release lag, so `releaseTimeliness` returns `n/a`; the latest quote can exist while the overview displays an older monthly value with no explanation. | Schedule the distinction in D1/D5, when dependency/version changes are already authorized, with a bilingual status contract and witness-cutoff tests. Otherwise mark R-C14 partially open and remove the claimed acceptance coverage. |
