docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:9:| 7 | P1 | §3.3、§3.5 | 驱动排序、并列规则和分解排序无法由现有契约唯一实现。`QuadrantView` 未定义 `score` 与存储 `scores` 的命名对应，`drivers` 的“目录序”也没有稳定 ID；`rank` 的 secondary/other 如何处理并列也未定义。客户端自行排序会形成与快照发布时不同的第二套结果解释。 | 服务端返回完整 `drivers` 及其排序依据，或明确唯一稳定排序键和并列规则：例如贡献降序、权重降序、`series_id` 字典序；secondary 由存储 `secondary_state` 决定，其余均为 other。冻结并测试完整 order。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:15:| 13 | P1 | §5.3–§5.5、§5.7、§10 | PR 顺序不可实施：D1 计划“一次目录 PR”同时包含 LPR/社融/MLF 核实结果和 active/missing 状态；D2–D4 又在 D1 后接入采集/解析，而且每次翻 status 都会产生新目录版本和 F4 v(n+1)。这与“避免 v2/v3/v4 连环”相矛盾，D2–D4 也没有各自的新方法版本计划。 | 明确目录状态与数据接入的版本策略。建议目录 PR 只新增稳定的 missing/restricted/weight-0 定义；任何把评分序列从 missing 改为 active 的 PR都同时创建对应 F4 方法版本并更新部署顺序。若坚持一次目录 PR，则把所有评分序列的采集、parser、fixture、事件和方法 v2一起完成，后续 PR不得再改这些目录行。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:21:| 19 | P1 | §5.2、§5.7 | 将 `catalogItemsOf` 从 `WEIGHTS_V1` 改为所有 indicators，并让 `displayInputsOf` 冻结所有 active 月/季频 weight-0 行，会改变快照 `observation_ids/history_ids/catalog_counts`。这不只是展示改动；F4 `gather` 要求所有 snapshot observation_ids 都可找到，且现有 replay/manifest/fixture hash 会被改。规格没有明确允许破坏这些冻结契约。 | 明确这是快照 manifest/schema 语义变更，并单独做快照版本/manifest migration；定义 F4 对 weight-0 observation 的输入处理、fixture 更新和历史回放兼容策略。若不能改变现有 snapshot 清单，则新增独立的 display manifest，而不是重写 regime snapshot。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:22:| 20 | P1 | §4.4 | 预设路由绕过既有分析 POST 的配额与保存语义，同时复用同一 `runAnalysis`，可能产生有副作用或高成本的分析。规格没有证明 `runAnalysis` 是纯函数，也没有列出 POST 路径中除 `request_id`、写库、计配额外的校验、权限、审计和限流语义。 | 提取并复用与 POST 完全相同的纯分析内核及所有输入验证；明确 preset 是服务端白名单、只读、无用户写入且不消耗用户配额的独立产品语义。若任一分析类型有外部调用或副作用，禁止在 preset 中运行。补齐授权、并发、LRU 隔离和每 preset 错误测试。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:27:| 25 | P1 | §3.5 | `ClockView` 把规则 `support` 与 `contribution` 都称为“四象限”，但 F4 v1 已用 `distribution` 且标注 `scores_are_not_probabilities`。本规格虽然禁用“概率”，没有禁用“置信度”等其他暗示模型可信度的语言，也无法保证规则标签本身不是判断。 | 所有展示文案明确写“规则得分/规则支持系数/规则归一化占比”；禁止“置信度、概率、预测概率、可靠度”；若展示 F4 分布，沿用 `scores_are_not_probabilities` 契约并显示非概率标记。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:31:| 29 | P2 | §3.3、§3.4 | `ClockRow.latest.unit` 被定义为必有字段，但 `latest` 可为 null；missing/restricted 行没有可用单位，示例又把 VIX 的单位/数据期显示为省略号，容易与缺失/受限混淆。 | 将 unit/period_end 放入 `latest` 或明确 nullable，并为每种状态规定“当前值/单位/数据期”的精确展示；受限但有公开元数据与完全不可见需拆成不同状态或明确字段来源。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:39:| 37 | P2 | §5.4 | `CN_AFRE_STOCK_YOY` 可由余额派生，但目录未明确新增 `CN_AFRE_STOCK` 的 ID、role、type、weight、source、unit和派生关系；若直接改现有行 active，评分类型 `liquidity_yoy` 与余额指数的语义无法同时成立。 | 明确余额原生行和同比派生行的稳定 ID、定义、单位、频率、weight、source、derive 和展示名称；评分只引用同比派生行。两者都进入目录时同步更新 exact-list 与方法版本。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/03-spec-round1-mmx.md:49:| 47 | P3 | §5.3–§5.5 | 规格把 `macro-events/2`、`cn-series/2`、`macro-transmission/2` 等版本 bump 与“不触碰冻结 manifest”并列，但没有定义这些版本在 API、数据库、fixture、缓存和旧快照中的兼容规则。 | 为每个配置版本定义稳定标识、读取优先级、旧版本保留期、API暴露字段和回放覆盖；只有方法/目录版本要求严格 pin 时才禁止 bump。 |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:3:| 1 | P1 | §2.4 D1 | **D1 bypasses existing publication conditions.** The flag permits the snapshot API to expose stored results, but P1 §3.2 explicitly requires F4 cards, forbids percentages without `display.percent`, and forbids fallback to macro numbers when F4 fails. F4 §4.1 makes `publishable` a licensing gate for **all judgment cards**, not merely probabilities. Showing scores while `publishable=false` contradicts these rules and the owner’s “只有满足既有发布条件才展示”. | Require the server flag **and** a publishable, eligible F4 judgment bound to the same snapshot/method before displaying judgment numbers. Explicitly revise P1’s percentage policy if non-probability score shares are desired; do not reinterpret the existing gate. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:5:| 3 | P1 | §§3.3–3.4 | `regionWeights(region)` reads **current code**, not snapshot-time weights. The proposed `{version, weights}` cannot truthfully claim historical provenance. Current catalog status/name/unit also misdescribes old snapshots after WP-D changes missing rows to active. A rules-version check does not catch catalog or methodology mismatch. | Read the catalog frozen under `snapshot.catalog_version` from `macro_catalog_versions`, select the matching methodology weights, and return frozen metadata. Reject unsupported versions explicitly. Iterate the complete historical weight set, including missing/restricted rows. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:7:| 5 | P2 | §§2.1, 3.3 | The comparison explanation is inaccurate: `typedChange` converts rate differences to **bp**, whereas the classifier uses percentage-point differences; FX d1 is a raw difference in `comparisons`, but a percentage change in `typedChange`. Also, §2.1 describes inflation-axis signs like growth-axis signs, while code uses the opposite inflation grouping. | Document rule-input value, unit and comparison period separately from display change. Correct the axis formula and footnote. Add examples for a 0.25pp/25bp yield move and FX d1/d3. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:11:| 9 | P2 | §2.4 | `macro_regime@v1` is **categorical**, with `scores_are_not_probabilities=true`. Its sample threshold/ECE parameter does not establish a future calibrated probability output. “After enough months, percent becomes available” is therefore an unsupported premise. | Remove the expected probability path for this method. Only render probability for a separately defined probability claim whose F4 display contract permits it; preserve categorical evaluation terminology. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:12:| 10 | P2 | §§3.5, 3.8 | The mandatory label “规则得分占比（非概率）” fails the proposed prohibition on `概率` everywhere except the F4 percent key. The new methodology rule table also lacks an explicit off-state mounting rule; placing strings under `judgment.*` does not prevent rendering them when disabled. | Exempt a narrowly defined non-probability disclaimer. Gate the methodology judgment section with the server-provided prop and test rendered off-state content. Preserve `pages.test.ts`’s literal prohibition throughout component files, including comments. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:13:| 11 | P1 | §§3.3, 5.7, 10 | Formula-hash drift begins in **WP-B**, not only WP-D: `macroRegimeV1.deps` explicitly includes `snapshots.ts`, which WP-B refactors. WP-D also changes other dependencies. Unchanged numerical output does not prevent `methodology-sync` refusing the changed hash. | Include a method-version/hash migration strategy for every PR touching the closure or declared dependencies. Test sync against the previously registered row, not merely fresh registration. Do not describe P5-B as independently safe without this dependency. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:15:| 13 | P1 | §§5.7, 8 | Removing v1 from `REGISTRY` avoids one sync comparison but does not preserve historical execution. v1 imports the mutable classifier/catalog, and `classifyAsOf` uses current catalog inputs. The spec changes v1 fixtures while claiming historical replay is unchanged. | Preserve original v1 fixtures and executable version bindings. Add v2 fixtures separately, define retirement explicitly, and prove that an existing v1 judgment can still replay/settle after the catalog upgrade—or state a concrete supported migration limitation. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:20:| 18 | P1 | §5.2 | WTREGEN is labelled `usd_bn`, with no conversion, but the primary series is **millions of U.S. dollars**, weekly ending Wednesday. This produces a 1,000× unit error and can quarantine valid values against the proposed 10,000 maximum. [FRED WTREGEN](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/WTREGEN) | Use `usd_mn` for native and derived WTREGEN, or introduce an explicit versioned ÷1,000 derivation with provenance. Test a known source value and its rendered unit. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:22:| 20 | P1 | §§5.3–5.5 | The migration plan targets a nonexistent `macro_series.adapter` CHECK. The actual adapter restriction is on `macro_evidence_objects.adapter`. It also omits the `macro_series.derive` CHECK for `effective_interval`, and changing the locator column CHECK alone leaves `macro_write_observations`’ locator allowlist rejecting `html_text`. | Enumerate and migrate the real table constraints and RPC validations. Include end-to-end database tests for official HTTP evidence, effective-interval catalog rows and native `html_text` observations. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:23:| 21 | P1 | §§5.3, 5.6 | Adding `official_http` functions to `cnSpecOf` is insufficient: `cnSeriesSpecs()` selects only `collectableOf('akshare')`, and `cnSpecOf` itself rejects other adapters. `worldbank_csv` has no complete type/provider/evidence/ingestion contract. | Define adapter routing through export, collector, ingest schema, parser, storage and freshness. Add a full evidence-to-observation test per adapter. Keep unimplemented sources missing with `source:null`. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:26:| 24 | P2 | §5.4 | The balance-derived AFRE fallback lacks a complete `CN_AFRE_STOCK` definition and a comparable-statistical-scope rule. Taking current balance divided by a year-earlier balance across an expansion of coverage can fabricate economic growth. A mutable native/derived fallback under one series definition also changes provenance semantics. | Define the balance series and units, pin the derivation policy, require comparable scope/vintage across both endpoints, and leave incompatible comparisons missing. Prefer the officially published growth rate when available. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/02-spec-round1-codex.md:27:| 25 | P2 | §§5.6, 10 | HK/World Bank rows have no resolved `region`, while TypeScript and SQL allow only US/CN. Pink Sheet monthly averages have no specified integration with daily/month-end historical boundaries. Adding rows alone also does not extend the frozen `CYCLE_COLUMNS_V1` list. | Decide regional assignment and average-price semantics before catalog insertion. Define units, quality rules and supported boundaries. If adding historical columns, introduce a new manifest configuration/version and fixture; preserve v1. |
docs/audits/2026-11-07-macro-p5/12-spec-round4-mmx.md:35:T-M35: still open (AFRE cross-page conflict, equal-date tie handling, and revision semantics remain undefined)
